thing. `vgt apply` validates the project path and directs you to this action rather than silently falling back to unsafe RPP editing.\n./README.md:36:checks the saved RPP and sidecar after both the first apply and re-apply.\n./README.md:41:apply action above. It resolves the reference track's source audio file,\n./README.md:42:runs the tempo/key/sections/chords detectors, and writes the results back\n./README.md:51:### Tempo & beat/downbeat grid\n./README.md:53:The `tempo` stage detects BPM, downbeat offset, and time signature from the\n./README.md:54:reference track's full mix, and fits either a single constant tempo or a\n./README.md:55:piecewise-linear tempo map (mode + residual are both recorded):\n./README.md:57:- **Primary backend: madmom**'s DBN beat + downbeat trackers, installed via\n./README.md:62:- **Fallback: librosa's `beat_track`** (installed by default) when madmom\n./README.md:63:  isn't installed, or fails to import. It gives beat times but no\n./README.md:64:  downbeats, so time signature falls back to a `time_signature_hint`\n./README.md:67:Every run also renders a **click-over-mix artifact** — `<project>.vgt-tempo-click.wav`,\n./docs/AGENTS.md:51:  regions, folders); only `[vgt]`-owned objects may be modified or removed.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:13:- a tempo map and downbeat grid (only where the project doesn't already have one — see the tempo-map rule below),\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:14:- song sections as `[vgt]` REAPER regions (intro/verse/chorus/…),\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:15:- detected key and beat-aligned chords as text items on a muted \"[vgt] Chords\" track,\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:20:**Non-goals for phase 1** (explicitly deferred): performance scoring, practice UI/looping logic (phase 2), tempo-ramped renders, tab generation (deprioritized in the source research as too error-prone to be the first investment), any hard cloud dependency — the default path uses LALAL.AI, but the tool must remain fully **offline-capable** via the Demucs fallback.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:35:│   • selected item → source path │             │  Demucs) → beats → key →   │\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:38:│  vgt_apply.lua                  │             └──────────┬─────────────────┘\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:42:└─────────────────────────────────┘        analysis/ manifest.json\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:49:- **The project is augmented by REAPER**, via `vgt_apply.lua` reading `manifest.json` — not by writing `.RPP` text. The API route can't corrupt the project, handles tempo-map/region/item construction correctly, and the same manifest contract feeds phase 2's practice controller later.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:50:- **Non-destructive and idempotent.** Everything vgt creates is `[vgt]`-prefixed (tracks, regions). Applying never deletes or renames anything it didn't create; re-applying first removes only its own `[vgt]` objects. All imported times are shifted by the analyzed item's position.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:51:- **Tempo-map rule** (the one genuinely invasive write — a project has exactly one tempo map): write it only if the project still has a single default tempo marker; otherwise leave the map untouched and ask, offering a muted \"[vgt] beats\" marker-item track as the non-invasive alternative.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:57:Each stage caches its output keyed on input-hash + settings, so correcting the tempo doesn't re-run 5 minutes of Demucs.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:63:| Beats/downbeats | madmom DBN beat + downbeat trackers | librosa `beat_track` (no downbeats) | madmom's NumPy-version pinning is fragile; isolate in its own extras group |\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:65:| Chords | madmom CNN chord recognition (maj/min vocabulary), labels then snapped to the beat grid | Chordino via sonic-annotator CLI | maj/min vocabulary won't capture 7ths/slash chords — acceptable for practice scaffolding, flagged in manifest |\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:68:| Package | write `manifest.json` + human-readable sidecars (`beats.txt`, `chords.lab`, `sections.txt`) | — | — |\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:72:Naively emitting one REAPER tempo marker per detected beat produces an unusable, jittery map. Instead:\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:74:1. Fit beat intervals; if variance is below a threshold, emit a **single constant BPM + downbeat offset** (covers most practice-worthy recordings, including anything cut to a click).\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:75:2. Otherwise fit **piecewise-linear tempo spans** and emit markers only at significant changes.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:76:3. Stem audio items are set **time-based, not beat-based**, so later tempo-map edits never stretch the audio.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:82:Auto-analysis *will* be wrong sometimes; the design treats correction as normal operation:\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:84:- `corrections.yaml` next to the manifest: tempo/key overrides, section renames and boundary nudges, chord fixes. Re-running the pipeline re-applies overrides and marks fields `human_verified: true`.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:85:- Every analysis stage emits a **checkable artifact**: a click-over-mix render for the beat grid, a printable chord sheet, a section timeline. Trust is earned per song, not assumed.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:96:  \"beats\":      {\"mode\": \"constant\", \"bpm\": 118.02, \"downbeat_offset_s\": 0.412,\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:97:                 \"time_signature\": \"4/4\", \"beat_times\": [\"...\"], \"human_verified\": false},\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:106:### Tracks added to the project by `vgt_apply.lua`\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:114:| [vgt] Chords | text items per chord segment | muted, locked |\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:116:Plus: `[vgt]` regions for sections, tempo map per the tempo-map rule, native metronome configured to the grid. The user's original song item/track is left untouched (they'll typically mute it in favor of the stems).\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:130:| M2 | Beat/tempo/downbeat grid + click-render verification artifact | click render sounds locked on 3 test songs, or the failure is visible and correctable via `corrections.yaml` | M |\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:131:| M3 | Key + beat-aligned chords + chord sheet artifact | chord sheet is usably close on the golden songs after ≤ a few corrections | M |\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:132:| M4 | Sections → regions + rename workflow | section boundaries within a bar or two; renaming is a one-file edit | S |\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:134:| M6 | `vgt_analyze.lua` + `vgt_apply.lua` against an **existing project** | end-to-end: select song item → analyze → project augmented per the table above; additive, idempotent re-apply; offset-shifted times; tempo-map rule honored; trimmed-item case refused cleanly | M |\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:137:Ordering rationale: the beat grid (M2) precedes chords/sections because both are expressed on the shared beat-synchronous grid — the same ordering the research recommends.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:144:- **Writing into a live user project**: the highest-consequence surface. Mitigated by the `[vgt]` prefix discipline, additive-only writes, idempotent re-apply, the tempo-map rule, and REAPER's undo block wrapping every apply.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:156:On the target machine: open an existing REAPER project containing a song item → run `vgt: Analyze selected item` → pipeline completes (LALAL stems + local analysis) → `vgt: Apply results` augments the project per the tables above, non-destructively and idempotently; corrections in `corrections.yaml` survive re-runs; all analysis provenance is in `manifest.json`. Then phase 2 (practice controller: stem muting, loop/tempo management, take recording) builds on the same manifest and the same `[vgt]` track conventions.\n./docs/phase0-live-verification.md:16:From the repository root, make a temporary copy that preserves the relative\n./docs/phase0-live-verification.md:18:it makes REAPER save after the apply action.\n./docs/phase0-live-verification.md:20:The apply action prompts for a reference track. To keep the run non-interactive,\n./docs/phase0-live-verification.md:36:uv run python scripts/verify_phase0_apply.py \"$PROJECT\" \\\n./docs/phase0-live-verification.md:39:# Repeat the exact select/apply/save sequence, then check it again for idempotency.\n./docs/phase0-live-verification.md:42:uv run python scripts/verify_phase0_apply.py \"$PROJECT\" \\\n./docs/phase0-live-verification.md:51:- the original name/GUID pairs and project sample rate, tempo, and time\n./docs/GOAL.md:39:  tempo/time-signature, and the existing track list (names and GUIDs) so vgt can tell which tracks are already\n./docs/GOAL.md:45:  every track/region vgt creates) so a student can immediately identify what vgt owns;\n./docs/GOAL.md:46:- **choosing a reference track and mirroring it** — the apply action asks which of the project's own tracks is\n./docs/GOAL.md:50:### Phase 1 — Reference analysis *(current)*\n./docs/GOAL.md:54:- **tempo & beat grid** — BPM, downbeat offset, and time signature;\n./docs/GOAL.md:57:- **chords** — beat-aligned chord labels (maj/min vocabulary).\n./docs/GOAL.md:60:- **an analysis stage in the CLI** — heavy analysis runs in the Python CLI, never inside REAPER; the ReaScript\n./docs/GOAL.md:62:- **persisting analysis in the sidecar** — extend the `<project>.vgt` schema (bump `schema_version`) to hold the\n./docs/GOAL.md:63:  detected tempo/key/sections/chords alongside phase 0's state;\n./docs/GOAL.md:64:- **reflecting analysis into the project**, additively and idempotently, as `[vgt]`-owned objects:\n./docs/GOAL.md:65:  - a **tempo map** — subject to the tempo-map rule: written only when the project still has a single default\n./docs/GOAL.md:66:    tempo marker; otherwise left untouched and offered non-invasively (a muted `[vgt]` beat-marker track);\n./docs/GOAL.md:67:  - `[vgt]` **section regions** (intro/verse/chorus/…), renamable by the user;\n./docs/GOAL.md:68:  - a **muted, locked `[vgt] Chords`** track carrying the beat-aligned chord labels as text items.\n./docs/GOAL.md:71:practice controls (stem muting / looping / tempo-ramp), and performance scoring. The full song-prep pipeline in\n./docs/GOAL.md:72:[phase1-song-prep-plan.md](phase1-song-prep-plan.md) is the longer-range roadmap; phase 1 here is its analysis\n./docs/GOAL.md:78:  Everything vgt creates carries the `[vgt]` prefix; only `[vgt]`-owned objects are ever touched. A re-apply\n./docs/GOAL.md:81:  do not fight the project's existing sample rate, tempo, etc.\n./docs/GOAL.md:86:- **Analysis stays out of the DAW process.** ML/DSP analysis runs in the Python CLI; REAPER only reads the\n./docs/GOAL.md:87:  reference source path and applies results through the API. The DAW never loads heavy analysis dependencies.\n./docs/GOAL.md:88:- **Correctable.** Auto-analysis will sometimes be wrong; every detected value (tempo, key, sections, chords) is\n./docs/GOAL.md:89:  overridable, and corrections survive re-runs of the analysis.\n./docs/GOAL.md:92:- **Idempotent.** Running the same command twice produces the same result — no duplicate tracks, folders, regions,\n./uv.lock:4:resolution-markers = [\n./uv.lock:71:    { name = \"standard-aifc\", marker = \"python_full_version >= '3.13'\" },\n./uv.lock:72:    { name = \"standard-sunau\", marker = \"python_full_version >= '3.13'\" },\n./uv.lock:93:    { name = \"pycparser\", marker = \"implementation_name != 'PyPy'\" },\n./uv.lock:368:    { name = \"standard-aifc\", marker = \"python_full_version >= '3.13'\" },\n./uv.lock:369:    { name = \"standard-sunau\", marker = \"python_full_version >= '3.13'\" },\n./uv.lock:621:    { name = \"colorama\", marker = \"sys_platform == 'win32'\" },\n./uv.lock:824:    { name = \"audioop-lts\", marker = \"python_full_version >= '3.13'\" },\n./uv.lock:825: